.TH NITRO 1 "October 2026" "nitro 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nitro \- interactive RDMA fabric monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nitro
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Nitro displays RDMA port throughput, driver counters, queue-pair process owners,
and ordinary network traffic using Linux netlink, sysfs and procfs.
The interface requires an 80 by 24 terminal. No RDMA hardware is required for demo mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --demo
Use explicitly labeled simulated devices and traffic.
.TP
.BI "--interval " MS
Sampling interval in milliseconds, from 100 to 60000. Default: 1000.
.TP
.BI "--device " NAMES
Comma-separated device names or device/port pairs.
.TP
.BI "--theme " NAME
Select midnight, forest or mono.
.TP
.B --ascii
Use ASCII borders and graphs.
.TP
.B --no-netlink
Read sysfs counters without RDMA netlink. Process owners are unavailable.
.TP
.B --json
Write one measured NDJSON sample by default.
.TP
.B --headless
Stream NDJSON until interrupted.
.TP
.BI "--count " N
Stop after N samples. Implies headless mode.
.TP
.BI "--duration " SECONDS
Stop after the given duration. Implies headless mode.
.TP
.BI "--record " PATH
Stream a Perfetto/Chrome JSON trace. Existing files are never overwritten.
.TP
.BI "--csv " PATH
Stream all counter totals and rates to CSV. Implies headless mode.
.TP
.B --help
Display command help.
.TP
.B --version
Display the version.
.SH KEYS
1/2 switches views. Arrows or j/k select rows. Tab switches focus.
Enter inspects counters or process details. / filters. s cycles sort; S reverses.
Space pauses display. a toggles averaging. g toggles graph scale.
+/- changes interval. t changes theme. r starts/stops recording.
w opens diagnostics; h opens help. q exits.
.SH COUNTERS
Missing and reset counters are unavailable, not zero. IB data counters are
four-byte words; canonical byte aliases are converted. Process rows indicate
QP ownership and do not estimate per-process bandwidth.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on successful completion or clean signal shutdown; 1 on a startup, argument,
or headless I/O error. Interactive collector errors are shown in diagnostics.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rdma (8),
.BR btop (1)
